				1882,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Consolidate workspace dispatch arms into WorkspacesRouter\n\nMove the inline `workspaces:*` match arms out of DispatchMatch.rs into a dedicated WorkspacesRouter module, continuing the consolidation pattern established by SearchRouter, ExtensionsRouter, and HistoryRouter in recent commits.\n\nThe new WorkspacesRouter::route() function centralises six workspace commands across four match arms — getFolders/getWorkspaceFolders/getWorkspace/getName delegate to EnterWorkspace, addFolder/addWorkspaceFolders delegate to CreateUntitledWorkspace, and removeFolder/removeWorkspaceFolders delegate to DeleteUntitledWorkspace — each with dev_log diagnostics and the standard Option<Result<Value, String>> return shape.\n\nPure structural consolidation — no behavioural change to workspace folder retrieval, creation, deletion, or naming semantics.",
			"SHA": "eabf64edbb131ae965bc470086ae1b33638dcf14"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T02:41:50Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1881,
				6
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Consolidate history dispatch into HistoryRouter, prune ExtensionsRouter comments\n\nRemove the seven inline `history:*` match arms from DispatchMatch.rs and delegate them through a dedicated HistoryRouter::route() function, mirroring the SearchRouter and ExtensionsRouter pattern introduced in preceding commits. The new module under Source/IPC/WindServiceHandlers/History/HistoryRouter.rs provides a unified match block returning Option<Result<Value, String>> with the standard unwrap_or_else(|| Ok(Value::Null)) fallback in the dispatch guard.\n\nClean up ExtensionsRouter.rs: collapse verbose per-arm doc comments into concise inline notes, switch import paths to use the local super-module short forms (ExtensionInstall::Fn vs crate::Extension::...), and pull arg_string from Utilities::JsonValueHelpers instead of the crate-level re-export.\n\nEnable web inspector (Inspect=1), recording (Record=1), and all-level tracing (Trace=all) in Info.plist for development debugging.\n\nPure structural consolidation and debug tooling — no behavioural change to extension, history, or IPC dispatch semantics.",
			"SHA": "28eed3f593a7b8741896e6ce75b1c90fa4c2e165"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T02:31:35Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1880,
				3
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Consolidate extension dispatch arms into ExtensionsRouter\n\nFollow the SearchRouter pattern (introduced in the preceding commits) to move the inline `extensions:*` match arms out of DispatchMatch.rs into a dedicated ExtensionsRouter module.\n\nThe new ExtensionsRouter::route() function in ExtensionsRouter.rs centralises all extension-host command handling — getAll, get, isActive, activate, getInstalled, scanSystemExtensions, scanUserExtensions, getUninstalled, query, search, download, install, uninstall, getManifest, reinstall, updateMetadata, and gallery-offline stubs — within a single match block returning Option<Result<Value, String>>. DispatchMatch.rs now delegates via a single `command if command.starts_with(\"extensions:\")` guard arm with the standard `unwrap_or_else(|| Ok(Value::Null))` fallback.\n\nLegacy dev_log argument-summary diagnostics, activation-event forwarding, argument override for system/user extension type coercion, and offline-gallery empty responses all move intact into the router. The Extensions.rs module index adds the public module declaration.\n\nPure structural consolidation — zero behavioural change to extension dispatch, activation, installation, or gallery semantics.",
			"SHA": "ea2e15c878c314cf1fb566cbe8d460eca2215b8a"
		}
	],
